  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1116 PM CDT Tue Jun 9 2026\n\nFriday a cold front will invade Middle Tennessee, bringing another \nround of showers and storms. Severe threat looks low with this \nsystem, but we could certainly see some strong storms with the \ninstability that is expected to be present. Guidance is also \nsuggesting high PWATs above 2\" again, so we will have to keep an eye \non moisture as we go into the weekend. Confidence is on the lower \nend with where stronger storms could develop though. \n\nPast Friday, there is not a whole lot of agreement in the models. \nLooks like rain chances will continue through early next week, but \nhard to say anything more specific than that. As the shorter term \nmodels grab a hold of the system, we should see improvement in this. \nBut it looks like the next few days are going to be the sunniest we \nmay see for a bit.",
